READING: the adaptive Hunter floor is a DEGREE-3 harvester (shared-endpoint pair
masses = weight-3 balanced relations anchored at the endpoint -- the leading sector
of monad's HYP-5097 degree gap).  Its EXACT ceiling is 3/7 at k=8 (doubling chains),
uniform value 6/49; both far below the honest bar 0.675.  Palindromic families have
W_top = W_bot EXACTLY (equal difference sets: min_j frac(-mx) over the same m-set),
so the 2-endpoint union gains NOTHING for the AP (the S62 palindrome symmetry in the
Hunter frame); spread families gain (union 0.55) but need no help.  Interior anchors
have mixed-sign differences whose pair masses can VANISH (THM-638 C2) => no degree-3
floor at all.  THE AP'S TAIL MASS IS CARRIED BY INTERIOR/ROTATING ANCHORS INVISIBLE
AT DEGREE 3: the responsible gap sits above the Farey-cell element q, which rotates
with the cell -- no fixed element carries it.  k=8 needs degree >= 4 or k-body tools.
